fix-symmetric-unique: compute 'unique' of every symmetric/keyed-hash object as a digest

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

TPM 2.0 Part 1, "Public Area Creation" (TPM_ALG_KEYEDHASH and
TPM_ALG_SYMCIPHER) requires unique := H_nameAlg(seedValue || sensitive) for
every keyed-hash and symmetric object. The reference uses an HMAC for
restricted decryption (parent) objects instead; that variant is disabled.

diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptUtil.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptUtil.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptUtil.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptUtil.c
@@ -1012,7 +1012,11 @@ void CryptComputeSymmetricUnique(
 {
     // For parents (symmetric and derivation), use an HMAC to compute
     // the 'unique' field
-    if(IS_ATTRIBUTE(publicArea->objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, restricted)
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // TPM 2.0 Part 1, "Public Area Creation", TPM_ALG_KEYEDHASH/TPM_ALG_SYMCIPHER,
+    // requires unique := H_nameAlg(obfuscate || key) for every keyed-hash and
+    // symmetric object, parents included, so the HMAC variant is disabled.
+    if(0 && IS_ATTRIBUTE(publicArea->objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, restricted)
        && IS_ATTRIBUTE(publicArea->objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, decrypt))
     {
         // Unique field is HMAC(sensitive->seedValue, sensitive->sensitive)
